===Report back to Aglaea{{subst:void|<!--104020912-->}}===
{{Dialogue Start}}

;(Unused &mdash; EnterDistrict_G{GroupID})
:{{tx}}
::'''Phainon:''' It's incredible to think that we returned {{Rubi|Nikador|Strife Titan}}'s Coreflame not so long ago... It wouldn't be an exaggeration to say that (Trailblazer) and your friend's arrival has melted the glaciers of history.
::{{Диалог|Стрелка}} This is what Trailblazing is.
::{{Диалог|Стрелка}} Where a Nameless goes, trouble follows.
::{{Диалог|Стрелка}} We've melted a real glacier before...
::'''Aglaea:''' You could say this is the true face of history. It slumbered for a thousand years, only to awaken for this one moment. Alas, now is not the time for a study of history.
::'''Aglaea:''' I do not see Anaxa around. Was this under your instructions, Phainon?
::'''Phainon:''' ...Yes. It just seems much more efficient than letting you two go at it endlessly.
::'''Aglaea:''' A rash decision. After all, he still bears a Coreflame with him.
::'''Aglaea:''' I do concur with your assessment of efficiency, though. Now, let us table the issue concerning him for the moment. The more urgent matter is the Coreflame of {{Rubi|Oronyx|Time Titan}}.
::'''Aglaea:''' The Chrysos Heirs had initially crafted a plan regarding the order to return the Coreflames. For Titans like Oronyx and {{Rubi|Cerces|Reason Titan}}, who harbor no intentions of harming humanity, our strategy entailed assuming their divinity only at the very end.
::'''Aglaea:''' But this unforeseen turn of events has thrown everything into disarray.
::'''Tribbie:''' If we don't return the Coreflames to the Vortex of Genesis and we leave the Titans' divine positions vacant... we can't even begin to imagine the disaster that would follow!
::'''Tribbie:''' But the most pressing issue at hand... {{Цвет|Ключевой|nobold=1|is that we haven't found the Chrysos Heir capable of bearing}} {{Rubi|{{Цвет|Ключевой|nobold=1|Oronyx}}|{{Цвет|Ключевой|nobold=1|Time Titan}}}}{{Цвет|Ключевой|nobold=1|'s divinity}}.
::'''Aglaea:''' Phainon, Castorice, Mydei, and Hyacine... Tribbie and I devoted a millennium scouring the world, only to find these few people.
::'''Aglaea:''' Only a chosen few possess the capacity to assume divinity, the elite among the Chrysos Heirs. We would never hastily extend our invitation without first verifying their potential to bear such power.
::'''Aglaea:''' Yet we cannot compel anyone into divinity, as it would be no different from sentencing them to the gallows.
::'''Phainon:''' Truly a dilemma...
::'''Tribbie:''' Yeah...
::'''Mem:''' Well...
::'''Mem:''' How about letting (Trailblazer) give it a try?
::{{Диалог|Стрелка}} I've been waiting for someone to say that, friend.
::{{Диалог|Стрелка}} So, you're okay with sentencing me to the gallows?
::{{Диалог|Стрелка}} The owner isn't liable for their pet's words.
::'''Mem:''' I'm serious! You're special to Amphoreus, and we all know that. Now, about {{Rubi|Oronyx|Time Titan}}...
::{{tx}}
:'''Aglaea:''' You've returned unscathed and brought tidings of triumph. Truly a moment worthy of celebration.
{{Dialogue End}}

